{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token, posts to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/track"},{"text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"), with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"text":", through a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, waiting ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": Mixpanel’s recommended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"},{"text":" for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":"; a record with no session is sent under its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own record identifier, with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"session’s events under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device:<session>"},{"type":"text","text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifier. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":" the record’s timestamp in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed one, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket"},{"type":"text","text":"), one of 255 properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, one tracked more than 119 hours before its batch is encoded or more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an hour after, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it finds no valid event in a request. The endpoint asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", so the answer’s body says so, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", and the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops the request and reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with Mixpanel’s error as the reason. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formed: it doesn’t confirm that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored. Check the project’s Live View after setting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination up."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, and answers 200 to an older one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while storing nothing. So the destination drops and reports such a record rather than send it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The encoder leaves out a record tracked more than 119 hours (5 days less an hour, for clocks that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disagree) before its batch is encoded, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Each request has a deadline 119 hours after its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest record was tracked, and a request still being retried when it passes isn’t sent again: it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is reported as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"text":". Pass the factory’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clock of your own to test this.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"MixpanelEncoding","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Mixpanel"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s "},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Why ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for the batch.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"title":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"title":"batchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of one event.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelRegion":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The data residency of a Mixpanel project, which decides the "},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint its events are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"posted to."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelregion","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelRegion","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"title":"MixpanelEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends batches to the Mixpanel project of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"projectToken"},{"type":"text","text":", whose data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resides in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"region"},{"type":"text","text":", through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/mixpanel(projecttoken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"projectToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"region"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16MixpanelEncoding0A6RegionO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MixpanelRegion"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ExponentialBackoff"},{"kind":"text","text":", "